                <pb facs="0773" n="669" sameAs="frus:frus1932v05/pg669"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.51/2483: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Munro</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Port-au-Prince</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-08-19T11:00:00-05:00">August 19, 1932—11
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 3:25 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>91. The Minister of Foreign Affairs suggested yesterday that the agreement
                    regarding the Haitianization of the Garde should also be dealt with as a
                    protocol to the treaty referred to in my telegram No. 83 and the Department’s
                    telegram No. 48.<anchor n="23" xml:id="d723-f1"/> In view of the probable
                    difficulty of obtaining prompt ratification for the financial agreement, I think
                    that it would be highly advisable to accept this suggestion. Please
                    instruct.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Munro</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
